⍝ benchmark: SHA-256 of 100 MiB (1 MiB of generated bytes, hashed 100 times over as one message)
Authored with the s2 shorthands (trith/s2/tools/trx.py); sha256.trh is generated by make bench-regen. ⍝
⍝ Words are 32-bit values held in ℤ, masked after every addition.

⍝ The Σ and σ functions rotate x by shifting y = x with a copy of itself in the high half:
bits 0…31 of y ≫ n are x rotated right by n, so three rotations cost three shifts and one mask ⍝
